    "blurb": "The show features a crisp Turn On Your Lovelight sandwich framing an acoustic interlude, then builds momentum with Alligator → Drums → The Other One into a soaring Mason’s Children jam. Phil’s bass is clear and tight while the dual drummers drive the extended improvisations. The soundboard capture is superb, making this a must‑listen performance.",
    "review": "On February 28, 1970 at the Family Dog on the Great Highway, the Dead delivered a uniquely structured set that still feels fresh today. A bright Turn On Your Lovelight sandwich bookends an acoustic interlude before the band launches into a high‑energy second half: Alligator segues into a tight drum duet, which then erupts into The Other One and rolls straight into a thunderous Mason’s Children jam. Highlights include the crisp lovelight rendition, the relentless momentum of the Alligator‑Drums‑Other One sequence, and the deep, non‑thumpy bass work that sits perfectly in the mix. Pigpen’s keyboards add color throughout, while Mickey Hart and Bill Kreutzmann power the jams with dynamic interplay. The recording, captured directly from the soundboard, is exceptionally clear—instrument separation is superb and there are no drop‑outs, allowing every nuance of this historic performance to shine.",
